Linux kernel, https://git.kernel.org (GPL-2.0)
  Releases ship a kernel inside the boot images techo5-boot-<version>.img (Echo Show 5 2nd gen,
  cronos) and techo5-boot-checkers-<version>.img (1st gen, checkers): Linux 4.9.337 for arm64. It is
  GPL-2.0, and this is where its source is.
    - Source: github.com/amazon-oss/android_kernel_amazon_mt8163, branch cronos/lineage-18.1, at
      commit 8d928c5176cc — the commit the LineageOS 18.1 boot image was built from (`uname -r` on
      the unit is 4.9.337-g8d928c5176cc). One commit serves both generations; the 1st gen has its own
      device trees in the same tree.
    - Configuration: cronos_defconfig for the 2nd gen, checkers_defconfig for the 1st, from that
      tree, with Bluetooth added. The resulting configurations are recorded in
      docs/dumps/cronos-lineage-kernel-4.9.337.config (as LineageOS ships it) and
      docs/dumps/cronos-techo5-kernel-4.9.337-bt.config (as TECHO5 builds it);
      docs/dumps/cronos-twrp-kernel-4.9.77.config is the TWRP kernel's, for comparison. All three are
      derived from that GPL-2.0 source and are GPL-2.0 themselves.
    - Changes: tools/linux/patches/checkers-0001-mic-enable-on-capture.patch, applied for the 1st gen
      build. It changes drivers/misc/gating.c, include/misc/gating.h and
      sound/soc/mediatek/mt_soc_audio_8163_amzn/mt_soc_machine.c so that releasing the mute latch
      brings the microphone path back, and is a modification of that GPL-2.0 source, so it is
      GPL-2.0 too. The appended device trees then have amzn,mic-downmix removed (tools/linux/
      patch-dtb.py).
    - The script that does all of it is tools/linux/build-kernel.sh, and docs/building.md is how to
      run it. A rebuild reproduces the shipped kernel.

Town names, echod/internal/feature/home/places.tsv.gz
  From GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), the cities5000 and cities15000 lists, licensed under
  the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Changes: reduced to places of 15,000 people or more, and of 5,000 or more in the U.S. and Canada;
  each kept as its name (in Latin letters where the screen's font has no others), latitude,
  longitude and population. The rain map credits GeoNames on screen.

Radar color tables, echod/internal/feature/home/radar_palettes.go
  The colors RainViewer's API documentation publishes for each radar reflectivity
  (https://www.rainviewer.com/files/rainviewer_api_colors_table.csv), and the palette of the Iowa
  Environmental Mesonet's national composite, used to read their tiles back into reflectivity.

Test audio, echod/internal/lib/denoise/testdata (not shipped in any release)
  Made by testdata/gen.py and this project's own: espeak-ng speech mixed with generated noise. The
  out_ files are the output of mmse_log_spu.py from
  https://github.com/vipchengrui/traditional-speech-enhancement (MIT, Copyright (c) 2019
  vipchengrui), which gen.py fetches and runs; that code is not copied into this repository.
